title: Claim registration to settlement
participant A "Agent / claims officer"
participant C "Claims module"
participant K "Second claims officer"
participant D "PostgreSQL"
participant RI "Reinsurance module"
A -> C: register claim (first notice of loss) with documents
C -> D: acceptance check: policy active, loss date inside the policy period; next_number('claim') -> CLM-
C -> D: claim registered; claim_history; claim_field_changes; handler assigned; notifications
C --> A: acknowledgement / letters generated as PDF on request
A -> C: review (in-review), update estimate and details (field-level audit)
A -> C: settle: amount, type, document
C -> D: pending-approval when approval is required (settlement awaiting a different user)
K -> C: approve / return / reject (maker cannot approve)
C -> D: approved -> settled (settled_amount, settled_at); later closed
RI -> D: recovery raised against the cession of the policy (reinsurance_recoveries)
note: Agents may register first notice of loss on their own policies only (record scope); review, reject, settle, approve and close need the claims role.
